# Phase 10 checks for outsourcing: partners and contracts (VS Code REST Client: click "Send Request" above a block).
# Start the API first (npm run dev:api) and load the sample data (npm run seed:api). Changes made here stay in
# the database: run npm run seed:api again afterwards.
#
# Every request needs an admin token: get one with the sign-in requests at the top of catalog.http and paste it
# into @adminToken below. A customer's token gets 403 FORBIDDEN, no token 401 UNAUTHENTICATED.
# Errors come back as { code, message, meta }.
#
# Sending a contract really sends it through the mail and SMS ports. With MAIL_DRIVER=log / SMS_DRIVER=log
# (development) nothing leaves the server: the text is printed on the API console as [EMAIL -> …] / [SMS -> …]
# and kept in the outbox table, and the answer's deliveryNote tells the admin to send it themselves.

@api = http://localhost:4000/api
@adminToken = paste-an-admin-token
@partner = op-001
@contract = oc-005
@event = paste-an-approved-to-confirmed-ref

### Every partner (how they are reached, contract counts), by service then name; ?includeArchived=true adds the archived
GET {{api}}/admin/outsource/partners
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Add a partner -> 201. An email or a mobile number is enough (neither: 400 on "email")
POST {{api}}/admin/outsource/partners
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Malvar Chairs", "service": "Chairs and tables", "contactPerson": "Ana Reyes", "email": "", "mobile": "0918 765 4321", "address": "", "notes": "" }

### Edit a partner -> the partner (the history lists the fields that changed)
PUT {{api}}/admin/outsource/partners/{{partner}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Batangas Party Rentals", "service": "Chairs and tables", "contactPerson": "Rico Delgado", "email": "rentals@batangaspartyrentals.ph", "mobile": "09171112233", "address": "Poblacion, Malvar, Batangas", "notes": "Delivers free within Malvar." }

### Archive or restore -> { count }. A partner with a contract waiting for their answer: 409 IN_USE
POST {{api}}/admin/outsource/partners/archive
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ids": ["op-006"], "archived": true }

### The bookings a contract can be for (approved to confirmed), soonest first
GET {{api}}/admin/outsource/events
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Every contract, newest first
GET {{api}}/admin/outsource/contracts
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### A new draft -> 201 (OUT-YYYY-#### from the counter). reservationRef "none" for no event; the amount is whole pesos
POST {{api}}/admin/outsource/contracts
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "partnerId": "{{partner}}", "reservationRef": "{{event}}", "items": [{ "name": "Monobloc chair", "qty": 50 }], "needBy": "2026-12-01", "amount": 2500, "notes": "" }

### Change a draft -> the contract. A sent contract: 423 LOCKED
PUT {{api}}/admin/outsource/contracts/{{contract}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "partnerId": "op-005", "reservationRef": "none", "items": [{ "name": "Round tablecloth", "qty": 12 }], "needBy": "2026-12-01", "amount": 4200, "notes": "" }

### Send (or send again): the same text to the partner's email and mobile number -> the contract with deliveryNote
### ('' when every channel went out). Each channel gets an outbox row; an archived partner: 400
POST {{api}}/admin/outsource/contracts/{{contract}}/send
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Tres Marias Catering Services · Outsourcing contract\n\nPlease supply 12 round tablecloths on 1 Dec 2026. Reply YES to accept." }

### The next status: accepted | declined | completed | cancelled (a decline or cancellation needs a 5+ character note)
POST {{api}}/admin/outsource/contracts/{{contract}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "accepted", "note": "Confirmed by text" }
